1
00:00:02,189 --> 00:00:10,189
Chapter 17 A week passed, and no news arrived of Mr. Rochester, ten days,

2
00:00:10,810 --> 00:00:12,229
and still he did not come.

3
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:17,790
Mrs. Fairfax said she should not be surprised if he were to go straight from

4
00:00:17,791 --> 00:00:21,652
the leaves to London, and thence to the continent, and

5
00:00:21,653 --> 00:00:25,229
not show his face again at Thornfield for a year to come.

6
00:00:26,279 --> 00:00:31,169
He had not unfrequently quitted it in a manner quite as abrupt and unexpected.

7
00:00:32,389 --> 00:00:37,889
When I heard this, I was beginning to feel a strange chill and failing at the heart.

8
00:00:40,009 --> 00:00:44,430
I was actually permitting myself to experience a sickening sense of

9
00:00:44,431 --> 00:00:50,830
disappointment, but rallying my wits and recollecting my principles, I at once

10
00:00:50,830 --> 00:00:56,430
called my sensations to order, and it was wonderful how I got over the

11
00:00:56,431 --> 00:01:00,776
temporary blunder, how I cleared up the mistake of supposing Mr.

12
00:01:00,777 --> 00:01:06,209
Rochester's movements, a matter in which I had any cause to take a vital interest.

13
00:01:07,319 --> 00:01:13,130
Not that I humbled myself by a slavish notion of inferiority, on the contrary,

14
00:01:13,930 --> 00:01:20,450
I just said, you have nothing to do with the master of Thornfield, further than to

15
00:01:20,451 --> 00:01:25,349
receive the salary he gives you for teaching his protégé, and to be grateful

16
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:29,367
for such respectful and kind treatment, as if you do

17
00:01:29,368 --> 00:01:33,610
your duty, you have a right to expect at his hands.

18
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:38,830
Be sure that is the only tie he seriously acknowledges between you and him,

19
00:01:39,709 --> 00:01:44,630
so don't make him the object of your fine feelings, your raptures, agonies,

20
00:01:44,790 --> 00:01:45,790
and so forth.

21
00:01:46,159 --> 00:01:52,529
He is not of your order, keep to your cast, and be too self-respecting to lavish

22
00:01:52,530 --> 00:01:55,578
the love of the whole heart, soul, and strength,

23
00:01:55,579 --> 00:01:59,069
where such a gift is not wanted and would be despised.

24
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:05,290
I went on with my day's business tranquilly, but ever and an on,

25
00:02:05,830 --> 00:02:10,509
vague suggestions kept wandering across my brain of reasons why I should quit

26
00:02:10,510 --> 00:02:15,200
Thornfield, and I kept involuntarily framing advertisements

27
00:02:15,201 --> 00:02:18,150
and pondering conjectures about new situations.

28
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:21,569
These thoughts I did not think to check.

29
00:02:22,669 --> 00:02:25,509
They might germinate and bear fruit if they could.

30
00:02:26,950 --> 00:02:32,310
Mr. Rochester had been absent upwards of a fortnight when the post brought Mrs.

31
00:02:32,509 --> 00:02:33,669
Fairfax a letter.

32
00:02:34,459 --> 00:02:38,509
It is from the master, said she, as she looked at the direction.

33
00:02:39,610 --> 00:02:44,430
Now I suppose we shall know whether we are to expect his return or not.

34
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:51,430
And while she broke the seal and peruse the document, I went on taking my coffee.

35
00:02:51,930 --> 00:02:52,930
We were at breakfast.

36
00:02:53,599 --> 00:02:57,201
It was hot, and I attributed to that circumstance

37
00:02:57,202 --> 00:03:00,689
a fiery glow which suddenly rose to my face.

38
00:03:01,790 --> 00:03:04,802
Why my hand shook, and why I involuntarily spilt

39
00:03:04,804 --> 00:03:07,389
half the contents of my cup into my saucer.

40
00:03:07,930 --> 00:03:09,229
I did not choose to consider.

41
00:03:11,189 --> 00:03:17,250
Well, I sometimes think we are too quiet, but we run a chance of being busy enough

42
00:03:17,251 --> 00:03:21,540
now, for a little while at least said Mrs. Fairfax,

43
00:03:21,541 --> 00:03:25,350
still holding the note before her spectacles.

44
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:29,049
Air I permitted myself to request an explanation.

45
00:03:29,750 --> 00:03:35,090
I tied the string of Del's pinnacle, which happened to be loose, having helped

46
00:03:35,091 --> 00:03:40,770
her also to another bun, and refilled her mug with milk, I said, nonchalantly.

47
00:03:42,270 --> 00:03:45,590
Mr. Rochester is not likely to return soon, I suppose.

48
00:03:47,229 --> 00:03:54,151
Indeed he is, in three days, he says, that will be next Thursday and not alone either.

49
00:03:55,189 --> 00:03:58,830
I don't know how many of the fine people at the leaves are coming with him.

50
00:03:59,759 --> 00:04:03,675
He sends directions for all the best bedrooms to be prepared,

51
00:04:03,676 --> 00:04:06,409
and the library and drawing rooms are to be cleaned out.

52
00:04:07,049 --> 00:04:09,691
I'm to get more kitchen hands from the George

53
00:04:09,692 --> 00:04:12,890
Inn at Millcoat, and from wherever else I can.

54
00:04:13,849 --> 00:04:16,659
And the ladies will bring their maids and the gentlemen

55
00:04:16,661 --> 00:04:19,889
their valleys, so we shall have a full house of it.

56
00:04:20,909 --> 00:04:26,090
And Mrs. Fairfax swallowed her breakfast, and hastened away to commence operations.

57
00:04:27,580 --> 00:04:31,349
The three days were, as she had foretold, busy enough.

58
00:04:32,985 --> 00:04:37,090
I had thought all the rooms at Thornfield beautifully clean and well arranged,

59
00:04:37,755 --> 00:04:39,630
but it appears I was mistaken.

60
00:04:40,750 --> 00:04:47,130
Three women were got to help, and such scrubbing, such brushing, such washing of

61
00:04:47,131 --> 00:04:51,950
paint and beating of carpets, such taking down and putting up of pictures,

62
00:04:52,939 --> 00:04:58,169
such polishing of mirrors and lustres, such lighting of fires in bedrooms,

63
00:04:59,209 --> 00:05:01,781
such air in of sheets and feather beds on

64
00:05:01,782 --> 00:05:05,771
hearths I never beheld, either before or since.

65
00:05:06,415 --> 00:05:09,189
Adele ran quite wild in the midst of it.

66
00:05:09,830 --> 00:05:12,540
The preparations for company and the prospect

67
00:05:12,541 --> 00:05:15,930
of their arrival seem to throw her into ecstasy.

68
00:05:17,259 --> 00:05:22,090
She would have Sophia to look over all her toilets, as she called frocks,

69
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:28,130
to furbish up any that were passays, and to air and arrange the new.

70
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:35,209
For herself, she did nothing but caper about in the front chambers, jump on and

71
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:39,549
off the bedsteads and lie on the mattresses and piled up bolsters and

72
00:05:39,550 --> 00:05:43,750
pillows before the enormous fires roaring in the chimneys.

73
00:05:45,090 --> 00:05:48,189
From school duties she was exonerated.

74
00:05:49,169 --> 00:05:53,790
Mrs. Fairfax had pressed me into her service, and I was all day in the

75
00:05:53,791 --> 00:05:59,569
storeroom, helping, or hindering her in the cook, learning to make custards and

76
00:05:59,570 --> 00:06:04,150
cheesecakes and French pastry, to trust game and garnish dessert dishes.

77
00:06:05,759 --> 00:06:11,971
The party were expected to arrive on Thursday afternoon, in time for dinner at six.

78
00:06:12,630 --> 00:06:16,729
During the intervening period, I had no time to nurse Cameras,

79
00:06:17,759 --> 00:06:22,310
and I believe I was as active and gay as anybody, Adele accepted.

80
00:06:23,389 --> 00:06:28,889
Still, now and then, I received a damping check to my cheerfulness, and was,

81
00:06:29,110 --> 00:06:35,169
in spite of myself, thrown back on the region of doubts and portance and dark

82
00:06:35,369 --> 00:06:36,369
conjectures.

83
00:06:37,459 --> 00:06:42,830
This was when I chanced to see the third story staircase door, which of late had

84
00:06:42,830 --> 00:06:48,709
always been kept locked, open slowly, and give passage to the form of grace

85
00:06:48,710 --> 00:06:53,229
pool, in prim cap, white apron, and handkerchief.

86
00:06:54,119 --> 00:07:00,311
When I watched her glide along the gallery, her quiet tread muffled in a list slipper.

87
00:07:00,970 --> 00:07:06,650
When I saw her look into the bustling, topsy-turvy bedrooms, just say a word,

88
00:07:06,810 --> 00:07:12,750
perhaps, to the charwoman about the proper way to polish a great, or clean a marble

89
00:07:12,751 --> 00:07:17,990
mantelpiece, or take stains from papered walls, and then pass on.

90
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:24,770
She would thus descend to the kitchen, once a day, eat her dinner, smoke a

91
00:07:24,771 --> 00:07:30,049
moderate pipe on the hearth, and go back, carrying her pot of porter with her,

92
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:35,029
for her private solace, in her own gloomy upper haunt.

93
00:07:37,090 --> 00:07:41,009
Only one hour in the twenty-four did she pass with her fellow servants below.

94
00:07:42,340 --> 00:07:45,068
All the rest of the time were spent in some

95
00:07:45,069 --> 00:07:48,190
low-sealed, oaken chamber of the second story.

96
00:07:49,169 --> 00:07:55,630
There she sat and sewed, and probably laughed drearily to herself, as

97
00:07:55,631 --> 00:07:58,330
companionless as a prisoner in his dungeon.

98
00:07:59,790 --> 00:08:06,090
The strangest thing of all was that not a soul in the house except me, noticed her

99
00:08:06,091 --> 00:08:10,970
habits, or seemed to marvel at them, no one discussed her position or

100
00:08:10,971 --> 00:08:14,849
employment, no one pitted her solitude or isolation.

101
00:08:15,779 --> 00:08:20,090
I once, indeed, overheard part of a dialogue between Leah and one of the

102
00:08:20,091 --> 00:08:23,069
charwoman, of which Grace formed the subject.

103
00:08:23,689 --> 00:08:28,029
Leah had been saying something I had not caught, and the charwoman remarked.

104
00:08:29,439 --> 00:08:31,189
She gets good wages, I guess?

105
00:08:32,509 --> 00:08:34,009
Yes, said Leah.

106
00:08:34,950 --> 00:08:38,770
I wish I had as good, not that minor to complain of.

107
00:08:39,669 --> 00:08:44,810
There's no stinginess at Thornfield, but they're not one fifth of the sum Mrs.

108
00:08:45,009 --> 00:08:48,130
Poole receives, and she is laying by.

109
00:08:49,110 --> 00:08:51,430
She goes every quarter to the bank at Millcoat.

110
00:08:52,889 --> 00:08:57,169
I should not wonder, but she has saved enough to keep her independent,

111
00:08:57,764 --> 00:08:58,770
if she like to leave.

112
00:08:59,970 --> 00:09:02,069
But I suppose she's got used to the place.

113
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:07,770
And then she's not 40 yet, and strong and able for anything.

114
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:10,849
It is too soon for her to give up business.

115
00:09:12,250 --> 00:09:15,549
She is a good hand, I dare say, said the charwoman.

116
00:09:16,380 --> 00:09:19,250
Ah, she understands what she has to do.

117
00:09:19,970 --> 00:09:23,789
Nobody better rejoind Leah significantly, and it is not

118
00:09:23,790 --> 00:09:27,810
everyone could fill her shoes, not for all the money she gets.

119
00:09:29,130 --> 00:09:31,669
That it is not, was the reply.

120
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:37,549
I wonder whether the master, the charwoman, was going on, but here Leah

121
00:09:37,550 --> 00:09:42,189
turned and perceived me, and she instantly gave her companion a nudge.

122
00:09:43,470 --> 00:09:45,990
Doesn't she know I heard the woman whisper.

123
00:09:47,450 --> 00:09:51,069
Leah shook her head, and the conversation was, of course, dropped.

124
00:09:51,950 --> 00:09:57,229
All I had gathered from it, amounted to this, that there was a mystery at

125
00:09:57,230 --> 00:10:02,830
Thornfield, and that from participation in that mystery I was purposely excluded.

126
00:10:03,909 --> 00:10:04,909
Thursday came.

127
00:10:05,750 --> 00:10:08,189
All work had been completed the previous evening.

128
00:10:09,009 --> 00:10:15,069
Carpets were laid down, bed hangings festooned, radiant white counter-pen is

129
00:10:15,070 --> 00:10:20,290
spread, toilet tables arranged, furniture rubbed, flowers piled in vases,

130
00:10:20,889 --> 00:10:25,209
both chambers and saloons looked as fresh and bright as hands could make them.

131
00:10:26,130 --> 00:10:33,490
The hall, too, was scoured, and the great carved clock, as well as the steps and

132
00:10:33,491 --> 00:10:38,049
banisters of the staircase, were polished to the brightness of glass.

133
00:10:38,985 --> 00:10:43,069
In the dining room, the sideboard flashed resplendent with plate.

134
00:10:43,950 --> 00:10:48,409
In the drawing room in Budwa, vases of exotics bloomed on all sides.

135
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:54,007
After noon arrived, Mrs. Fairfax assumed her best

136
00:10:54,008 --> 00:10:57,670
black satin gown, her gloves and her gold watch.

137
00:10:58,810 --> 00:11:04,630
For it was her part to receive the company, to conduct the ladies to their rooms, etc.

138
00:11:05,509 --> 00:11:09,158
A del too would be dressed, though I thought she had little

139
00:11:09,159 --> 00:11:12,290
chance of being introduced to the party that day at least.

140
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:19,529
However, to please her, I allowed Sophie to apparel her in one of her short,

141
00:11:19,830 --> 00:11:21,650
full muslin frocks.

142
00:11:22,189 --> 00:11:25,349
For myself, I had no need to make any change.

143
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,930
I should not be called upon to quit my sanctum of the schoolroom.

144
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:35,349
For a sanctum, it was now become to me, a very pleasant refuge in time of trouble.

145
00:11:37,450 --> 00:11:43,610
It had been a mild, serene spring day, one of those days which, towards the end

146
00:11:43,611 --> 00:11:49,390
of March or the beginning of April, rise shining over the earth as heralds of summer.

147
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:55,430
It was drawing to an end now, but the evening was even warm, and I sat at work

148
00:11:55,779 --> 00:11:57,610
in the schoolroom with the window open.

149
00:11:58,979 --> 00:12:04,610
It gets late, said Mrs. Fairfax, entering in rustling state.

150
00:12:05,779 --> 00:12:10,549
I am glad I ordered dinner, an hour after the time Mr. Rochester mentioned.

151
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:13,369
For it is past six now.

152
00:12:14,610 --> 00:12:18,709
I have sent John down to the gates to see if there is anything on the road.

153
00:12:19,669 --> 00:12:23,770
One can see a long way from thence in the direction of Mill Court.

154
00:12:24,819 --> 00:12:25,819
She went to the window.

155
00:12:27,009 --> 00:12:28,950
Here he is, said she.

156
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:32,689
Well, John, leaning out.

157
00:12:33,409 --> 00:12:34,409
Any news?

158
00:12:36,549 --> 00:12:38,770
Their coming man was the answer.

159
00:12:39,669 --> 00:12:40,909
They'll be here in ten minutes.

160
00:12:42,659 --> 00:12:44,430
A del flew to the window.

161
00:12:45,729 --> 00:12:51,770
I followed, taking care to stand on one side, so that, screened by the curtain,

162
00:12:52,590 --> 00:12:54,349
I could see without being seen.

163
00:12:55,639 --> 00:13:00,709
The ten minutes John had given seemed very long, but at last wheels were heard.

164
00:13:01,490 --> 00:13:07,569
Four equestrians galloped up the drive, and after them came two open carriages.

165
00:13:08,729 --> 00:13:12,189
Fluttering veils and waving plumes filled the vehicles.

166
00:13:12,935 --> 00:13:16,029
Two of the Cavaliers were young, dashing looking gentlemen.

167
00:13:16,889 --> 00:13:20,729
The third was Mr. Rochester, on his black horse, Mesrour.

168
00:13:21,470 --> 00:13:22,869
Pilot bounding before him.

169
00:13:23,630 --> 00:13:28,669
At his side rode a lady, and he and she were the first of the party.

170
00:13:29,959 --> 00:13:33,049
Her purple riding habit almost swept the ground.

171
00:13:33,889 --> 00:13:39,689
Her veil streamed long on the breeze, mingling with its transparent folds and

172
00:13:39,690 --> 00:13:43,229
glee through them, shone rich raven ringlets.

173
00:13:45,159 --> 00:13:50,830
Miss Ingram exclaimed Mrs. Fairfax, and a way she hurried to her post below.

174
00:13:52,330 --> 00:13:55,531
The Cavalcade, following the sweep of the drive, quickly

175
00:13:55,532 --> 00:13:58,950
turned the angle of the house, and I lost sight of it.

176
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:05,689
A del now petitioned to go down, but I took her on my knee, and gave her to

177
00:14:05,690 --> 00:14:10,889
understand that she must not on any account think of venturing inside of the

178
00:14:10,890 --> 00:14:16,770
ladies, either now or at any other time, unless expressly sent for.

179
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:20,810
That Mr. Rochester would be very angry, etc.

180
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:25,575
Some natural tears she shared on being told this, but as I

181
00:14:25,576 --> 00:14:29,990
began to look very grave, she consented at last to wipe them.

182
00:14:30,990 --> 00:14:33,549
A joyous stir was now audible in the hall.

183
00:14:34,369 --> 00:14:39,310
Gentleman's deep tones and ladies' silvery accents blent harmoniously together,

184
00:14:39,970 --> 00:14:44,909
and distinguishable above all, though not loud, was the sonorous voice of

185
00:14:44,911 --> 00:14:51,250
the master of Thornfield Hall, welcoming his fair and gallant guests under its roof.

186
00:14:52,909 --> 00:14:56,889
Then light steps ascended the stairs, and there was a tripping through the

187
00:14:56,890 --> 00:15:01,669
gallery, and soft, cheerful laughs, and opening and closing doors,

188
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:04,409
and for a time, a hush.

189
00:15:27,325 --> 00:15:32,750
et habile les dams, et qu'est-ce qui a mis son, comme celle-là on apprend.

190
00:15:34,389 --> 00:15:36,130
Don't you feel hungry, Adele?

191
00:15:37,310 --> 00:15:41,750
May we, mademoiselle, while our single sister is con nous n'avons pas mange.

192
00:15:42,930 --> 00:15:46,382
Well, now, while the ladies are in their rooms,

193
00:15:46,383 --> 00:15:49,569
I will venture down and get you something to eat.

194
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:56,110
And issuing from my asylum with precaution, I sought a backstairs,

195
00:15:56,650 --> 00:15:58,650
which conducted directly to the kitchen.

196
00:15:59,509 --> 00:16:02,110
All in that region was fire and commotion.

197
00:16:02,930 --> 00:16:07,970
The soup and fish were in the last stage of projection, and the cook hung over her

198
00:16:07,971 --> 00:16:13,509
crucibles in a frame of mind and body, threatening, spontaneous combustion.

199
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:19,330
In the servant's hall, two coachmen and three

200
00:16:19,330 --> 00:16:22,840
gentlemen's gentlemen stood or sat around the fire.

201
00:16:23,755 --> 00:16:26,939
The abbergales, I suppose, were upstairs with their mistresses.

202
00:16:28,110 --> 00:16:33,080
The new servants that had been hired from milk-coat were bustling about everywhere.

203
00:16:34,099 --> 00:16:38,180
Threading this chaos, I at last reached the ladder.

204
00:16:39,470 --> 00:16:43,420
There I took possession of a cold chicken, a roll of

205
00:16:43,421 --> 00:16:47,680
bread, some tarts, a plate or two, and a knife and fork.

206
00:16:48,979 --> 00:16:52,299
With this booty, I made a hasty retreat.

207
00:16:53,669 --> 00:16:58,000
I had regained the gallery, and was just shutting the back door behind me,

208
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:01,204
when an accelerated hum warned me that the

209
00:17:01,205 --> 00:17:04,861
ladies were about to issue from their chambers.

210
00:17:06,310 --> 00:17:09,779
I could not proceed to the schoolroom without passing some of their doors,

211
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:14,680
and running the risk of being surprised with my cargo of vitilage.

212
00:17:15,919 --> 00:17:22,279
So I stood still at this end, which, being windowless, was dark, quite dark

213
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:25,500
now, for the sun was set and twilight gathering.

214
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:31,099
Presently, the chambers gave up their fair tenants one after another.

215
00:17:32,060 --> 00:17:37,240
Each came out galey and airy, with dress that gleamed lustrous through the dusk.

216
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:42,819
For a moment, they stood grouped together at the other extremity of the gallery,

217
00:17:43,599 --> 00:17:47,459
conversing in a key of sweet, subdued vivacity.

218
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:54,279
They then descended the staircase, almost as noiselessly as a bright mist

219
00:17:54,529 --> 00:17:55,580
rolls down a hill.

220
00:17:56,759 --> 00:18:01,159
Their collective appearance had left on me an impression of high-born elegance,

221
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:04,020
such as I had never before received.

222
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:14,180
I found a cried she in English.

223
00:18:14,990 --> 00:18:16,700
Oh, I wish I might go to them.

224
00:18:17,540 --> 00:18:21,159
Do you think Mr. Rochester will send for us by and by after dinner?

225
00:18:22,650 --> 00:18:24,619
No, indeed, I don't.

226
00:18:25,490 --> 00:18:28,720
Mr. Rochester has something else to think about.

227
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:31,720
Never mind the ladies tonight.

228
00:18:32,700 --> 00:18:34,299
Perhaps you will see them tomorrow.

229
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:36,340
Here is your dinner.

230
00:18:37,950 --> 00:18:40,995
She was really hungry, so the chicken and tart

231
00:18:40,996 --> 00:18:44,820
served to divert her attention for a time.

232
00:18:45,759 --> 00:18:52,299
It was well I secured this forage, or both she, I, and Sophie, to whom I

233
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:57,820
conveyed a share of our repast, would have run a chance of getting no dinner at all.

234
00:18:58,639 --> 00:19:02,020
Everyone downstairs was too much engaged to think of us.

235
00:19:03,020 --> 00:19:07,941
The dessert was not carried out till after 9, and at 10 footmen

236
00:19:07,942 --> 00:19:11,680
were still running too and fro with trays and coffee cups.

237
00:19:13,380 --> 00:19:18,599
I allowed Adele to sit up much later than usual, for she declared she could not

238
00:19:18,650 --> 00:19:21,582
possibly go to sleep while the doors kept opening

239
00:19:21,583 --> 00:19:24,400
and shutting below and people bustling about.

240
00:19:25,310 --> 00:19:28,741
Besides, she added, a message might possibly

241
00:19:28,742 --> 00:19:32,181
come from Mr. Rochester when she was undressed.

242
00:19:35,569 --> 00:19:39,378
I told her stories as long as she would listen to them,

243
00:19:39,379 --> 00:19:42,520
and then for a change I took her out into the gallery.

244
00:19:44,299 --> 00:19:49,639
The hall lamp was now lit and it amused her to look over the ballast raid and

245
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:53,180
watch the servants passing backwards and forwards.

246
00:19:54,569 --> 00:19:59,439
When the evening was far advanced, a sound of music issued from the drawing

247
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:03,724
room, whether the piano had been removed, Adele and

248
00:20:03,725 --> 00:20:07,119
I sat down on the top step of the stairs to listen.

249
00:20:08,029 --> 00:20:12,225
Presently, a voice blent with the rich tones of the instrument,

250
00:20:12,226 --> 00:20:15,659
it was a lady who sang, and very sweet her notes were.

251
00:20:16,459 --> 00:20:20,393
The solo over, a duet followed, and then a glee, a

252
00:20:20,394 --> 00:20:23,500
joyous, conversational murmur filled up the intervals.

253
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:25,520
I listened long.

254
00:20:26,849 --> 00:20:32,220
Suddenly I discovered that my ear was wholly intent on analysing the mingled

255
00:20:32,221 --> 00:20:38,139
sounds, and trying to discriminate amidst the confusion of accents, those of Mr.

256
00:20:38,319 --> 00:20:39,319
Rochester.

257
00:20:39,770 --> 00:20:44,659
And when it caught them, which it soon did, it found a further task in framing

258
00:20:44,661 --> 00:20:49,400
the tones rendered by distance inarticulate into words.

259
00:20:50,650 --> 00:20:51,759
The clock struck eleven.

260
00:20:52,950 --> 00:20:58,580
I looked at Adele, whose head lent against my shoulder, her eyes were waxing heavy,

261
00:20:59,430 --> 00:21:02,200
so I took her up in my arms and carried her off to bed.

262
00:21:04,310 --> 00:21:07,619
It was near one before the gentlemen and ladies sought their chambers.

263
00:21:08,990 --> 00:21:12,080
The next day was as fine as its predecessor.

264
00:21:13,380 --> 00:21:18,661
It was devoted by the party to an excursion to some sight in the neighbourhood.

265
00:21:19,740 --> 00:21:25,060
They set out early in the forenoon, some on horseback, the rest in carriages.

266
00:21:25,869 --> 00:21:28,439
I witnessed both the departure and the return.

267
00:21:29,240 --> 00:21:35,207
Miss Ingram, as before, was the only lady equestrian, and, as before, Mr.

268
00:21:35,407 --> 00:21:37,340
Rochester galloped at her side.

269
00:21:38,340 --> 00:21:40,599
The two rode a little apart from the rest.

270
00:21:42,009 --> 00:21:44,373
I pointed out this circumstance to Mrs.

271
00:21:44,375 --> 00:21:48,120
Fairfax, who was standing at the window with me.

272
00:21:49,540 --> 00:21:53,759
You said it was not likely they should think of being married, said I.

273
00:21:54,779 --> 00:21:59,139
But you see Mr. Rochester evidently prefers her to any of the other ladies.

274
00:22:00,709 --> 00:22:04,159
Yes, I dare say, no doubt he admires her.

275
00:22:05,349 --> 00:22:07,259
And she, him, I added.

276
00:22:08,319 --> 00:22:13,520
Look how she leans her head towards him, as if she were conversing confidentially.

277
00:22:14,319 --> 00:22:15,779
I wish I could see her face.

278
00:22:15,959 --> 00:22:17,619
I have never had a glimpse of it yet.

279
00:22:19,069 --> 00:22:22,360
You will see her this evening, answered Mrs. Fairfax.

280
00:22:23,305 --> 00:22:27,520
I happened to remark to Mr. Rochester how much Adele wished to be introduced to the

281
00:22:27,521 --> 00:22:32,580
ladies, and he said, oh, let her come into the drawing room after dinner,

282
00:22:33,080 --> 00:22:35,220
and request Mrs. Air to accompany her.

283
00:22:36,520 --> 00:22:42,299
Yes, he said that from mere politeness, I need not go I am sure, I answered.

284
00:22:43,825 --> 00:22:50,740
Well, I observed to him that as you were unused to company, I did not think you

285
00:22:50,741 --> 00:22:53,799
would like appearing before so gay a party all

286
00:22:53,800 --> 00:22:58,599
strangers, and he replied, in his quick way, nonsense.

287
00:22:59,544 --> 00:23:04,200
If she objects, tell her it is my particular wish, and if she resists,

288
00:23:04,740 --> 00:23:07,279
say I shall come and fetch her in case of consummacy.

289
00:23:09,110 --> 00:23:12,099
I will not give him that trouble, I answered.

290
00:23:12,970 --> 00:23:16,240
I will go, if no better, maybe, but I don't like it.

291
00:23:17,250 --> 00:23:18,919
Shall you be there, Mrs. Fairfax?

292
00:23:19,869 --> 00:23:23,479
No, I pleaded off, and he admitted my plea.

293
00:23:24,724 --> 00:23:29,099
I will tell you how to manage, so as to avoid the embarrassment of making

294
00:23:29,100 --> 00:23:33,459
a formal entrance, which is the most disagreeable part of the business.

295
00:23:34,250 --> 00:23:36,954
You must go into the drawing room, while it is

296
00:23:36,955 --> 00:23:39,721
empty, before the ladies leave the dinner table.

297
00:23:40,279 --> 00:23:42,799
Choose your seat in any quiet nook you like.

298
00:23:43,909 --> 00:23:48,419
You need not stay long after the gentleman come in, unless you please.

299
00:23:49,270 --> 00:23:56,120
Just let Mr. Rochester see you are there, and then slip away, nobody will notice you.

300
00:23:57,240 --> 00:23:59,340
Will these people remain long, do you think?

301
00:24:00,900 --> 00:24:03,919
Perhaps two or three weeks, certainly not more.

302
00:24:05,130 --> 00:24:12,000
After the Easter recess, Sir George Lynn, who was lately elected member for Milcoat,

303
00:24:12,509 --> 00:24:14,680
will have to go up to town and take his seat.

304
00:24:15,659 --> 00:24:18,720
I dare say Mr. Rochester will accompany him.

305
00:24:20,069 --> 00:24:25,279
It surprises me that he has already made so protracted a stay at Thornfield.

306
00:24:26,919 --> 00:24:32,177
It was with some trepidation that I perceived the hour approach

307
00:24:32,179 --> 00:24:35,580
when I was to repair with my charge to the drawing room.

308
00:24:36,845 --> 00:24:41,139
A del had been in a state of ecstasy all day, after hearing

309
00:24:41,140 --> 00:24:44,159
she was to be presented to the ladies in the evening.

310
00:24:45,389 --> 00:24:47,236
And it was not till Sophie commenced the

311
00:24:47,237 --> 00:24:50,841
operation of dressing her that she sobered down.

312
00:24:51,569 --> 00:24:56,799
Then the importance of the process quickly stedded her, and by the time she had her

313
00:24:56,800 --> 00:25:02,540
curls arranged in well-smooth drooping clusters, her pink satin frock put on,

314
00:25:03,040 --> 00:25:06,639
her long sash tied, and her lace mittens adjusted.

315
00:25:07,340 --> 00:25:09,419
She looked as grave as any judge.

316
00:25:10,139 --> 00:25:13,259
No need to warn her not to disarrange her attire.

317
00:25:14,169 --> 00:25:19,779
When she was dressed, she sat demurely down in her little chair, taking care

318
00:25:19,780 --> 00:25:24,759
previously to lift up the satin skirt, for fear she should crease it,

319
00:25:25,279 --> 00:25:28,860
and assured me she would not stir thence till I was ready.

320
00:25:30,729 --> 00:25:35,880
This I quickly was, my best dress, the silver gray one, purchased for Miss

321
00:25:35,881 --> 00:25:40,220
Temple's wedding, and never worn since, was soon put on.

322
00:25:41,099 --> 00:25:47,060
My hair was soon smoothed, my sole ornament, the pearl brooch soon assumed.

323
00:25:48,080 --> 00:25:49,080
We descended.

324
00:25:49,860 --> 00:25:54,299
Fortunately, there was another entrance to the drawing room than that through the

325
00:25:54,300 --> 00:25:56,680
saloon, where they were all seated at dinner.

326
00:25:57,970 --> 00:25:59,340
We found the apartment vacant.

327
00:26:00,349 --> 00:26:06,060
A large fire burning silently on the marble hearth, and wax candles shining in

328
00:26:06,061 --> 00:26:11,459
bright solitude amid the exquisite flowers with which the tables were adorned.

329
00:26:12,580 --> 00:26:14,759
The crimson curtain hung before the arch.

330
00:26:15,900 --> 00:26:17,878
Slighters was the separation this drapery

331
00:26:17,879 --> 00:26:21,201
formed from the party in the adjoining saloon.

332
00:26:21,759 --> 00:26:24,779
They spoke in so low a key that nothing of their

333
00:26:24,780 --> 00:26:29,159
conversation could be distinguished beyond a soothing murmur.

334
00:26:29,915 --> 00:26:33,649
A del, who appeared to be still under the influence of

335
00:26:33,650 --> 00:26:38,159
a most solemnizing impression, sat down without a word.

336
00:26:38,799 --> 00:26:41,139
On the footstool, I pointed out to her.

337
00:26:41,849 --> 00:26:48,760
I retired to a window seat, and taking a book from a table near, endeavoured to read.

338
00:26:48,959 --> 00:26:50,860
A del brought her stool to my feet.

339
00:26:51,610 --> 00:26:53,580
A long she touched my knee.

340
00:26:55,319 --> 00:26:56,319
What is it, Adel?

341
00:27:06,080 --> 00:27:10,720
You think too much of your toilet, Adel, but you may have a flower.

342
00:27:11,810 --> 00:27:15,360
And I took a rose from a vase and fastened it in her sash.

343
00:27:16,319 --> 00:27:19,301
She sighed a sigh of ineffable satisfaction,

344
00:27:19,302 --> 00:27:22,180
as if her cup of happiness were now full.

345
00:27:23,180 --> 00:27:26,599
I turned my face away to conceal a smile I could not suppress.

346
00:27:27,959 --> 00:27:32,039
There was something ludicrous as well as painful in the little

347
00:27:32,040 --> 00:27:36,299
Parisienne's earnest and innate devotion to matters of dress.

348
00:27:37,509 --> 00:27:40,340
A soft sound of rising now became audible.

349
00:27:48,400 --> 00:27:53,459
The curtain was down light on the silver and glass of a magnificent dessert service

350
00:27:53,860 --> 00:27:55,180
covering a long table.

351
00:27:55,819 --> 00:27:57,840
A band of ladies stood in the opening.

352
00:27:58,479 --> 00:28:01,860
They entered, and the curtain fell behind them.

353
00:28:02,970 --> 00:28:07,244
There were but eight, yet somehow, as they flocked

354
00:28:07,245 --> 00:28:11,459
in, they gave the impression of a much larger number.

355
00:28:11,959 --> 00:28:17,340
Some of them were very tall, many were dressed in white, and all had a sweeping

356
00:28:17,341 --> 00:28:24,061
amplitude of ray that seemed to magnify their persons as a mist magnifies the moon.

357
00:28:25,250 --> 00:28:27,060
I rose and curtsied to them.

358
00:28:27,860 --> 00:28:29,659
One or two bent their heads in return.

359
00:28:30,520 --> 00:28:32,319
The others only stared at me.

360
00:28:33,119 --> 00:28:38,560
They dispersed about the room, reminding me by the lightness and buoyancy

361
00:28:38,561 --> 00:28:42,860
of their movements, of a flock of white plumey birds.

362
00:28:44,060 --> 00:28:49,080
Some of them threw themselves in half -reclining positions on the sofas and

363
00:28:49,080 --> 00:28:54,080
ottomans, some bent over the tables, and examined the flowers and books.

364
00:28:55,220 --> 00:28:57,740
The rest gathered in a group around the fire.

365
00:28:58,650 --> 00:29:03,459
All talked in a low but clear tone, which seemed habitual to them.

366
00:29:04,279 --> 00:29:08,479
I knew their names afterwards, and may as well mention them now.

367
00:29:09,290 --> 00:29:12,779
First, there was Mrs. Eston and two of her daughters.

368
00:29:13,750 --> 00:29:19,240
She had evidently been a handsome woman, and was well preserved still, of her

369
00:29:19,241 --> 00:29:22,919
daughters, the eldest Amy, was rather little.

370
00:29:23,740 --> 00:29:28,720
Naive, and childlike in face and manner, and peacont in form.

371
00:29:29,400 --> 00:29:32,340
Her white muslin dress and blue sash became her well.

372
00:29:33,319 --> 00:29:37,459
The second, Luisa, was taller and more elegant in figure.

373
00:29:38,130 --> 00:29:43,979
With a very pretty face, of that order, the French term Minouashifan, both sisters

374
00:29:44,430 --> 00:29:45,430
were fair as lilies.

375
00:29:46,549 --> 00:29:52,520
Lady Lynn was a large and stout personage of about 40, very erect, very haughty

376
00:29:52,521 --> 00:29:56,819
looking, richly dressed in a satin robe of changeful sheen.

377
00:29:57,689 --> 00:30:00,611
Her dark hair shone glossily under the shade of an

378
00:30:00,612 --> 00:30:04,159
azure plume, and within the circlet of a band of gems.

379
00:30:06,430 --> 00:30:11,220
Mrs. Colonel Dent was less showy, but I thought more lady-like.

380
00:30:12,119 --> 00:30:18,139
She had a slight figure, a pale gentle face and fair hair, her black satin dress,

381
00:30:18,840 --> 00:30:24,139
her scarf of rich foreign lace, and her pearl ornaments, pleased me better

382
00:30:24,140 --> 00:30:26,380
than the rainbow radiance of the title Dame.

383
00:30:27,955 --> 00:30:32,799
But the three most distinguished, partly perhaps, because the tallest

384
00:30:32,800 --> 00:30:40,060
figures of the band, were the Dowager Lady Ingram and her daughters Blanche and Mary.

385
00:30:41,130 --> 00:30:44,200
They were all three of the loftiest stature of women.

386
00:30:45,340 --> 00:30:47,840
The Dowager might be between 40 and 50.

387
00:30:48,659 --> 00:30:50,000
Her shape was still fine.

388
00:30:50,830 --> 00:30:54,200
Her hair, by candlelight at least, still black.

389
00:30:55,119 --> 00:30:58,520
Her teeth too were still apparently perfect.

390
00:30:59,389 --> 00:31:04,400
Most people would have termed her a splendid woman of her age, and so she was,

391
00:31:04,659 --> 00:31:06,180
no doubt, physically speaking.

392
00:31:07,319 --> 00:31:10,713
But then, there was an expression of almost

393
00:31:10,715 --> 00:31:14,819
insupportable haughtiness in her bearing and countenance.

394
00:31:15,610 --> 00:31:21,439
She had Roman features and a double chin, disappearing into a throat like a pillar.

395
00:31:22,180 --> 00:31:26,360
These features appeared to me, not only inflated and darkened,

396
00:31:26,915 --> 00:31:32,880
but even furrowed with pride, and the chin was sustained by the same principle in a

397
00:31:32,881 --> 00:31:35,880
position of almost preternatural erectness.

398
00:31:37,470 --> 00:31:41,159
She had, likewise, a fierce and a hard eye.

399
00:31:41,799 --> 00:31:43,500
It reminded me of Mrs. Reeds.

400
00:31:44,080 --> 00:31:45,819
She mouthed her words in speaking.

401
00:31:46,669 --> 00:31:47,669
Her voice was deep.

402
00:31:48,435 --> 00:31:53,959
Its inflections very pompous, very dogmatical, very intolerable, in short.

403
00:31:55,509 --> 00:32:00,799
A crimson velvet robe, and a shawl turban of some gold-raught Indian fabric,

404
00:32:01,580 --> 00:32:06,479
invested her, I suppose she thought, with a truly imperial dignity.

405
00:32:07,319 --> 00:32:11,779
Blanche and Mary were of equal stature, straight and tall as poplars.

406
00:32:12,599 --> 00:32:16,900
Mary was too slim for her height, but Blanche was molded like a dianne.

407
00:32:17,759 --> 00:32:20,279
I regarded her, of course, with special interest.

408
00:32:21,819 --> 00:32:26,166
First, I wished to see whether her appearance accorded with Mrs.

409
00:32:26,167 --> 00:32:27,861
Fairfax's description?

410
00:32:28,369 --> 00:32:33,759
Secondly, whether it at all resembled the fancy miniature I had painted of her.

411
00:32:34,580 --> 00:32:37,700
And thirdly, it will out.

412
00:32:38,840 --> 00:32:43,240
Whether it were such as I should fancy likely to suit Mr. Rochester's taste.

413
00:32:44,240 --> 00:32:49,619
As far as person went, she answered point for point, both to my picture and Mrs.

414
00:32:49,740 --> 00:32:50,880
Fairfax's description.

415
00:32:51,849 --> 00:32:55,384
The noble bust, the sloping shoulders, the graceful

416
00:32:55,385 --> 00:32:58,540
neck, the dark eyes and black ringlets were all there.

417
00:32:59,580 --> 00:33:00,580
But her face.

418
00:33:01,599 --> 00:33:05,560
Her face was like her mothers, a youthful unfurried likeness,

419
00:33:06,119 --> 00:33:10,500
the same low brow, the same high features, the same pride.

420
00:33:11,490 --> 00:33:13,959
It was not, however, so satanine a pride.

421
00:33:14,939 --> 00:33:16,200
She laughed continually.

422
00:33:16,740 --> 00:33:19,310
Her laugh was satirical, and so was the habitual

423
00:33:19,311 --> 00:33:21,980
expression of her arched and haughty lip.

424
00:33:24,590 --> 00:33:26,840
Genius is said to be self-conscious.

425
00:33:28,424 --> 00:33:33,139
I cannot tell whether Mrs. Ingram was a genius, but she was self-conscious,

426
00:33:33,740 --> 00:33:35,439
remarkably self-conscious indeed.

427
00:33:36,419 --> 00:33:41,020
She entered into a discourse on botany with the gentle Mrs. Dent.

428
00:33:42,150 --> 00:33:46,061
It seemed Mrs. Dent had not studied that science, though,

429
00:33:46,062 --> 00:33:50,520
as she said, she liked flowers, especially wild ones.

430
00:33:51,400 --> 00:33:54,580
Mrs. Ingram had, and she ran over its vocabulary with an air.

431
00:33:55,849 --> 00:34:01,043
I presently perceived she was what is vernaculately termed, trailing Mrs.

432
00:34:01,843 --> 00:34:04,259
Dent, that is, playing on her ignorance.

433
00:34:05,240 --> 00:34:09,479
Her trail might be clever, but it was decidedly not good-natured.

434
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:11,000
She played.

435
00:34:11,619 --> 00:34:13,299
Her execution was brilliant.

436
00:34:14,040 --> 00:34:15,040
She sang.

437
00:34:15,279 --> 00:34:16,340
Her voice was fine.

438
00:34:16,779 --> 00:34:19,753
She talked French, apart to her mama, and she

439
00:34:19,754 --> 00:34:22,741
talked it well, with fluency and with a good accent.

440
00:34:23,810 --> 00:34:27,400
Mary had a milder and more open countenance than Blanche.

441
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:32,700
Softer features, too, and a skin some shades fairer.

442
00:34:33,470 --> 00:34:38,360
Mrs. Ingram was dark as a spaniard, but Mary was deficient in life.

443
00:34:39,290 --> 00:34:41,979
Her face lacked expression, her eye -luster.

444
00:34:42,479 --> 00:34:45,865
She had nothing to say, and having once taken a

445
00:34:45,866 --> 00:34:49,341
seat, remained fixed like a statue in its niche.

446
00:34:50,479 --> 00:34:53,400
The sisters were both attired in spotless white.

447
00:34:54,759 --> 00:34:57,551
And did I now think Mrs. Ingram's such a choice

448
00:34:57,552 --> 00:35:01,080
as Mr. Rochester would be likely to make?

449
00:35:01,360 --> 00:35:02,360
I could not tell.

450
00:35:03,369 --> 00:35:05,580
I did not know his taste in female beauty.

451
00:35:06,490 --> 00:35:10,217
If he liked the majestic, she was the very type

452
00:35:10,218 --> 00:35:13,990
of majesty, then she was accomplished, sprightly.

453
00:35:15,279 --> 00:35:19,369
Most gentlemen would admire her, I thought, and that he did admire her,

454
00:35:20,119 --> 00:35:22,069
I already seem to have obtained proof.

455
00:35:23,299 --> 00:35:28,470
To remove the last shade of doubt, it remained, but to see them together.

456
00:35:29,650 --> 00:35:32,685
You are not to suppose, reader, that Adele has all this

457
00:35:32,686 --> 00:35:35,549
time been sitting motionless on the stool at my feet?

458
00:35:36,189 --> 00:35:37,189
No.

459
00:35:37,259 --> 00:35:42,689
When the ladies entered, she rose advanced to meet them, made a stately reverence,

460
00:35:43,279 --> 00:35:46,849
and said with gravity, bonjour midams.

461
00:35:48,150 --> 00:35:52,130
And Mrs. Ingram had looked down at her with a mocking air and exclaimed,

462
00:35:52,549 --> 00:35:54,049
oh, what a little puppet!

463
00:35:54,979 --> 00:35:56,610
Lady Lynn had remarked.

464
00:35:57,419 --> 00:36:01,930
It is Mr. Rochester's ward, I suppose, the little French girl he was speaking of.

465
00:36:03,349 --> 00:36:10,310
Mrs. Dent had kindly taken her hand and given her a kiss, Amy and Louisa Eston had

466
00:36:10,311 --> 00:36:14,229
cried out simultaneously, what a love of a child.

467
00:36:15,654 --> 00:36:21,650
And then they had called her to a sofa, where she now sat in sconce between them,

468
00:36:22,450 --> 00:36:28,130
chattering alternately in French and broken English, absorbing not only the

469
00:36:28,131 --> 00:36:32,138
young ladies' attention, but that of Mrs. Eston and

470
00:36:32,139 --> 00:36:35,490
Lady Lynn, and getting spoilt to her heart's content.

471
00:36:37,189 --> 00:36:41,009
At last coffee is brought in, and the gentlemen are summoned.

472
00:36:42,209 --> 00:36:43,290
I sit in the shade.

473
00:36:44,229 --> 00:36:47,304
If any shade there be in this brilliantly lit

474
00:36:47,305 --> 00:36:50,850
apartment, the window curtain half hides me.

475
00:36:51,549 --> 00:36:54,450
Again, the arch-yorns, they come.

476
00:36:55,419 --> 00:36:59,029
The collective appearance of the gentlemen, like that of the ladies,

477
00:36:59,794 --> 00:37:01,090
is very imposing.

478
00:37:02,069 --> 00:37:06,090
They are all costumed in black, most of them are tall, some young,

479
00:37:06,770 --> 00:37:10,458
Henry and Frederick Lynn are very dashing sparks

480
00:37:10,459 --> 00:37:14,270
indeed, and Colonel Dent is a fine soldierly man.

481
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:20,509
Mr. Eston, the magistrate of the district, is gentlemen like.

482
00:37:21,090 --> 00:37:25,790
His hair is quite white, his eyebrows and whiskers still dark, which gives him

483
00:37:25,791 --> 00:37:28,990
something of the appearance of a pair noble de théâtre.

484
00:37:30,259 --> 00:37:33,950
Lord Ingram, like his sisters, is very tall.

485
00:37:34,630 --> 00:37:40,311
Like them also, he is handsome, but he shares Mary's apathetic and listless look.

486
00:37:41,150 --> 00:37:45,709
He seems to have more length of limb than vivacity of blood or vigor of brain.

487
00:37:47,220 --> 00:37:48,430
And where is Mr. Rochester?

488
00:37:49,869 --> 00:37:50,869
He comes in last.

489
00:37:51,819 --> 00:37:55,310
I am not looking at the arch, yet I see him enter.

490
00:37:56,229 --> 00:37:59,236
I try to concentrate my attention on those netting

491
00:37:59,237 --> 00:38:02,270
needles, on the meshes of the purse I am forming.

492
00:38:03,060 --> 00:38:07,290
I wish to think only of the work I have in my hands, to see

493
00:38:07,291 --> 00:38:10,750
only the silver beads and silk threads that lie in my lap.

494
00:38:11,729 --> 00:38:15,279
Whereas, I distinctly behold his figure, and I

495
00:38:15,280 --> 00:38:19,010
inevitably recall the moment when I last saw it.

496
00:38:19,979 --> 00:38:24,169
Just after I had rendered him, what he deemed an essential service.

497
00:38:25,250 --> 00:38:31,049
And he, holding my hand, and looking down on my face, surveyed me with eyes that

498
00:38:31,050 --> 00:38:33,970
revealed a heart full and eager to overflow.

499
00:38:35,029 --> 00:38:37,290
In whose emotions I had a part.

500
00:38:38,540 --> 00:38:40,810
How near had I approached him at that moment?

501
00:38:41,990 --> 00:38:47,150
What had occurred since, calculated to change his and my relative positions?

502
00:38:48,819 --> 00:38:54,438
Yet now, how distant, how far estranged we were, so far

503
00:38:54,439 --> 00:38:57,950
estranged, that I did not expect him to come and speak to me.

504
00:38:58,959 --> 00:39:04,150
I did not wonder when, without looking at me, he took a seat at the other side of

505
00:39:04,151 --> 00:39:07,650
the room and began conversing with some of the ladies.

506
00:39:09,080 --> 00:39:14,529
No sooner did I see that his attention was riveted on them, and that I might gaze

507
00:39:14,530 --> 00:39:20,049
without being observed, then my eyes were drawn involuntarily to his face.

508
00:39:21,299 --> 00:39:24,152
I could not keep their lids under control, they

509
00:39:24,153 --> 00:39:27,631
would rise, and the irids would fix on him.

510
00:39:27,860 --> 00:39:34,150
I looked and had an acute pleasure in looking, a precious yet poignant pleasure,

511
00:39:34,860 --> 00:39:40,950
pure gold, with a steely point of agony, a pleasure like what the thirst perishing

512
00:39:40,951 --> 00:39:45,175
man might feel who knows the well to which he has crept is

513
00:39:45,176 --> 00:39:48,729
poisoned, yet stoops and drinks divine drafts nevertheless.

514
00:39:50,990 --> 00:39:55,330
Most true is it that beauty is in the eye of the gayser.

515
00:39:56,290 --> 00:40:02,090
My master's colourless, olive face, square massive brow, broad and jetty

516
00:40:02,091 --> 00:40:08,290
eyebrows deep eyes, strong features firm, grim mouth, all energy decision will.

517
00:40:09,860 --> 00:40:14,790
Were not beautiful, according to rule, but they were more than beautiful to me.

518
00:40:15,709 --> 00:40:19,950
They were full of an interest, an influence that quite mastered me,

519
00:40:20,790 --> 00:40:24,830
that took my feelings from my own power and fettered them in his.

520
00:40:26,240 --> 00:40:28,229
I had not intended to love him.

521
00:40:29,090 --> 00:40:32,136
The reader knows I had wrought hard to extirpate

522
00:40:32,137 --> 00:40:35,070
from my soul, the germs of love they're detected.

523
00:40:36,139 --> 00:40:39,534
And now, at the first renewed view of him,

524
00:40:39,536 --> 00:40:43,811
they spontaneously arrived, green and strong.

525
00:40:44,569 --> 00:40:46,669
He made me love him without looking at me.

526
00:40:48,159 --> 00:40:50,650
I compared him with his guests.

527
00:40:51,919 --> 00:40:57,069
What was the gallant grace of the lins, the languid elegance of Lord Ingram,

528
00:40:57,790 --> 00:41:01,532
even the military distinction of Colonel Dent, contrasted

529
00:41:01,533 --> 00:41:05,110
with his look of native pith and genuine power.

530
00:41:06,400 --> 00:41:09,689
I had no sympathy in their appearance, their expression.

531
00:41:10,790 --> 00:41:15,250
Yet I could imagine that most observers would call them attractive, handsome,

532
00:41:15,569 --> 00:41:19,068
imposing, while they would pronounce Mr. Rochester

533
00:41:19,069 --> 00:41:21,889
at once harsh featured and melancholy looking.

534
00:41:23,569 --> 00:41:25,430
I saw them smile, laugh.

535
00:41:26,490 --> 00:41:27,490
It was nothing.

536
00:41:28,090 --> 00:41:31,950
The light of the candles had as much soul in it as their smile,

537
00:41:31,951 --> 00:41:35,529
the tinkle of the bell as much significance as their laugh.

538
00:41:36,639 --> 00:41:38,310
I saw Mr. Rochester smile.

539
00:41:39,250 --> 00:41:40,889
His stern features softened.

540
00:41:41,590 --> 00:41:44,209
His eye grew both brilliant and gentle.

541
00:41:45,049 --> 00:41:47,389
Its ray, both searching and sweet.

542
00:41:48,470 --> 00:41:52,409
He was talking at the moment to Luisa and Amy Eshton.

543
00:41:53,750 --> 00:41:56,224
I wondered to see them receive with calm,

544
00:41:56,225 --> 00:41:59,311
that look, which seemed to me so penetrating.

545
00:41:59,680 --> 00:42:03,569
I expected their eyes to fall, the color to rise under it.

546
00:42:04,430 --> 00:42:07,689
Yet I was glad when I found they were in no sense moved.

547
00:42:09,169 --> 00:42:11,909
He is not to them what he is to me, I thought.

548
00:42:12,869 --> 00:42:14,169
He is not of their kind.

549
00:42:15,099 --> 00:42:16,630
I believe he is of mine.

550
00:42:17,470 --> 00:42:18,750
I am sure he is.

551
00:42:19,299 --> 00:42:20,490
I feel akin to him.

552
00:42:21,110 --> 00:42:24,229
I understand the language of his countenance and movements.

553
00:42:25,490 --> 00:42:30,669
Though rank and wealth sever us widely, I have something in my brain and heart,

554
00:42:31,029 --> 00:42:34,970
in my blood and nerves, that assimilates me mentally to him.

555
00:42:36,250 --> 00:42:40,050
Did I say a few days since, that I had nothing to

556
00:42:40,051 --> 00:42:43,790
do with him but to receive my salary at his hands?

557
00:42:45,310 --> 00:42:49,369
Did I forbid myself to think of him in any other light than as a paymaster?

558
00:42:50,310 --> 00:42:51,790
Blast for me against nature.

559
00:42:52,610 --> 00:42:56,810
Every good, true, vigorous feeling I have gathers impulsively around him.

560
00:42:58,669 --> 00:43:00,869
I know I must conceal my sentiments.

561
00:43:01,880 --> 00:43:02,970
I must smother hope.

562
00:43:03,610 --> 00:43:06,430
I must remember that he cannot care much for me.

563
00:43:07,500 --> 00:43:10,870
For when I say that I am of his kind, I do not mean that

564
00:43:10,871 --> 00:43:14,729
I have his force to influence and his spell to attract.

565
00:43:15,979 --> 00:43:19,310
I mean only that I have certain tastes and feelings in common with him.

566
00:43:20,130 --> 00:43:24,750
I must then repeat continually that we are forever-sundered.

567
00:43:25,540 --> 00:43:29,349
And yet, while I breathe and think, I must love him.

568
00:43:31,185 --> 00:43:32,185
Coffee is handed.

569
00:43:32,909 --> 00:43:37,250
The ladies, since the gentleman entered, have become lively as larks.

570
00:43:37,810 --> 00:43:39,810
Conversation whacks his brisk and merry.

571
00:43:40,369 --> 00:43:42,869
Colonel Dent and Mr. Eston argue on politics.

572
00:43:43,590 --> 00:43:44,770
Their wives listen.

573
00:43:45,669 --> 00:43:51,110
The two proud dowagers, Lady Lynn and Lady Ingram, can fabulate together.

574
00:43:52,310 --> 00:43:59,049
Sir George, whom by the by, I have forgotten to describe, a very big and very

575
00:43:59,050 --> 00:44:02,736
fresh looking country gentleman, stands before their

576
00:44:02,737 --> 00:44:06,970
sofa, coffee cup in hand, and occasionally puts in a word.

577
00:44:08,279 --> 00:44:11,965
Mr. Frederick Lynn has taken a seat beside Mary Ingram,

578
00:44:11,966 --> 00:44:15,610
and is showing her the engravings of a splendid volume.

579
00:44:16,599 --> 00:44:20,849
She looks, smiles now and then, but apparently says little.

580
00:44:21,779 --> 00:44:25,926
The tall and flagmatic Lord Ingram leans with folded

581
00:44:25,927 --> 00:44:29,830
arms on the chairback of the little and lively Amy Eston.

582
00:44:30,790 --> 00:44:33,610
She glances up at him and chatters like a wren.

583
00:44:34,479 --> 00:44:36,750
She likes him better than she does Mr. Rochester.

584
00:44:38,189 --> 00:44:42,349
Henry Lynn has taken possession of an ottoman at the feet of Luisa.

585
00:44:43,750 --> 00:44:45,229
Adele shares it with him.

586
00:44:45,990 --> 00:44:49,889
He is trying to talk French with her, and Luisa laughs at his blunders,

587
00:44:50,779 --> 00:44:52,869
with whom will Blanche Ingram pair.

588
00:44:54,069 --> 00:44:58,650
She is standing alone at the table, bending gracefully over an album.

589
00:44:59,470 --> 00:45:03,750
She seems waiting to be sought, but she will not wait too long.

590
00:45:04,509 --> 00:45:06,810
She herself selects a mate.

591
00:45:07,549 --> 00:45:14,509
Mr. Rochester, having quitted the Estons, stands on the table.

592
00:45:15,409 --> 00:45:19,650
She confronts him, taking her station on the opposite side of the mantelpiece.

593
00:45:21,205 --> 00:45:25,689
Mr. Rochester, I thought you were not fond of children, nor am I.

594
00:45:27,330 --> 00:45:30,477
Then what induced you to take charge of such

595
00:45:30,478 --> 00:45:34,271
a little doll as that, pointing to Adele?

596
00:45:34,709 --> 00:45:35,810
Where did you pick her up?

597
00:45:36,965 --> 00:45:38,130
I did not pick her up.

598
00:45:41,189 --> 00:45:42,970
She was sent her to school.

599
00:45:43,790 --> 00:45:44,889
I could not afford it.

600
00:45:45,330 --> 00:45:46,490
Schools are so dear.

601
00:45:47,770 --> 00:45:50,069
Why, I suppose you have a governess for her.

602
00:45:50,909 --> 00:45:52,590
I saw a person with her just now.

603
00:45:52,990 --> 00:45:53,990
Is she gone?

604
00:45:54,380 --> 00:45:57,770
Oh no, there she is still behind the window curtain.

605
00:45:58,990 --> 00:46:00,130
You pay her, of course.

606
00:46:00,869 --> 00:46:03,549
I should think it quite as expensive, more so.

607
00:46:04,430 --> 00:46:06,209
For you have them both to keep in addition.

608
00:46:07,529 --> 00:46:13,069
I feared, or should I say, hoped, the illusion to me would make Mr.

609
00:46:13,209 --> 00:46:16,846
Rochester glance my way, and I involuntarily shrank

610
00:46:16,847 --> 00:46:20,470
farther into the shade, but he never turned his eyes.

611
00:46:22,580 --> 00:46:28,451
I have not considered the subject, said he indifferently, looking straight before him.

612
00:46:29,090 --> 00:46:32,889
No, you men never do consider economy and common sense.

613
00:46:33,779 --> 00:46:36,430
You should hear Mama on the chapter of governesses.

614
00:46:37,229 --> 00:46:42,529
Mary and I have had, I should think, a dozen at least in our day, half of them

615
00:46:42,530 --> 00:46:46,590
detestable and the rest ridiculous, and all incubi.

616
00:46:47,029 --> 00:46:48,029
Were they not Mama?

617
00:46:49,915 --> 00:46:50,950
Did you speak my own?

618
00:46:51,990 --> 00:46:54,842
The young lady thus claimed as the Dowager's special

619
00:46:54,843 --> 00:46:57,470
property, reiterated her question with an explanation.

620
00:46:58,610 --> 00:47:00,970
My dearest, don't mention governesses.

621
00:47:01,974 --> 00:47:03,049
The word makes me nervous.

622
00:47:03,979 --> 00:47:07,470
I have suffered a martyrdom from their incompetency and caprice.

623
00:47:08,470 --> 00:47:10,729
I thank heaven I have now done with them.

624
00:47:12,194 --> 00:47:17,590
Mrs. Dent here bent over to the pious lady and whispered something in her ear.

625
00:47:18,380 --> 00:47:21,780
I suppose, from the answer elicited, it was a reminder

626
00:47:21,781 --> 00:47:25,389
that one of the enathematized race was present.

627
00:47:26,560 --> 00:47:28,830
Tont Pee said her lady ship.

628
00:47:29,549 --> 00:47:30,830
I hope it may do her good.

629
00:47:32,000 --> 00:47:37,270
Then, in a lower tone but still loud enough for me to hear, I noticed her.

630
00:47:37,569 --> 00:47:42,729
I am a judge of physiognomy, and in hers I see all the faults of her class.

631
00:47:43,779 --> 00:47:44,849
What are they, madam?

632
00:47:45,849 --> 00:47:47,470
Inquired Mr. Rochester allowed.

633
00:47:48,849 --> 00:47:53,123
I will tell you in your private ear, replied she, wagging

634
00:47:53,125 --> 00:47:56,009
her turban three times with potenta's significance.

635
00:47:57,310 --> 00:47:59,729
But my curiosity will be passed its appetite.

636
00:48:00,409 --> 00:48:01,569
It craves food now.

637
00:48:02,970 --> 00:48:03,970
Ask Blanche.

638
00:48:04,569 --> 00:48:05,750
She is nearer you than I.

639
00:48:06,985 --> 00:48:08,990
Oh, don't refer him to me, mamma.

640
00:48:10,034 --> 00:48:12,569
I have just one word to say of the whole tribe.

641
00:48:13,659 --> 00:48:15,009
They are a nuisance.

642
00:48:15,950 --> 00:48:17,930
Not that I ever suffered much from them.

643
00:48:18,709 --> 00:48:20,349
I took care to turn the tables.

644
00:48:21,400 --> 00:48:25,555
What tricks Theodore and I used to play on our Miss Wilson's and Mrs.

645
00:48:25,556 --> 00:48:27,470
Grey's and Madam Zubair's?

646
00:48:28,610 --> 00:48:31,290
Mary was always too sleepy to join in a plot with spirit.

647
00:48:32,255 --> 00:48:34,790
The best fun was with Madam Zubair.

648
00:48:35,799 --> 00:48:40,655
Miss Wilson was a poor sickly thing, lacry moss and low

649
00:48:40,656 --> 00:48:44,529
spirited, not worth the trouble of vanquishing in short.

650
00:48:45,689 --> 00:48:48,069
And Mrs. Grey was coarse and insensible.

651
00:48:48,889 --> 00:48:50,209
No blow took effect on her.

652
00:48:52,130 --> 00:48:53,590
But poor Madam Zubair.

653
00:48:55,130 --> 00:49:00,509
I see her yet in her raging passions when we had driven her to extremities,

654
00:49:01,349 --> 00:49:05,630
spilt our tea, crumbled our bread and butter, tossed our books up to the

655
00:49:05,631 --> 00:49:11,389
ceiling, and played a chari-vari with the ruler and desk, the fender and fire ions.

656
00:49:12,259 --> 00:49:15,229
Theodore, do you remember those merry days?

657
00:49:16,529 --> 00:49:22,810
Yes, to be sure I do, drilled Lord Ingram, and the poor old stick used to cry out.

658
00:49:23,630 --> 00:49:25,729
Oh, you villains, childs.

659
00:49:26,599 --> 00:49:31,150
And then we surmanized her on the presumption of attempting to teach such

660
00:49:31,151 --> 00:49:34,810
clever blades as we were when she was herself so ignorant.

661
00:49:36,330 --> 00:49:37,330
We did.

662
00:49:38,090 --> 00:49:43,549
And to do you know, I helped you in prosecuting, or persecuting, your tutor.

663
00:49:44,490 --> 00:49:49,229
Way faced Mr. Vining, the person in the pip, as we used to call him.

664
00:49:50,169 --> 00:49:53,389
He and Miss Wilson took the liberty of falling in love with each other.

665
00:49:54,029 --> 00:49:55,849
At least Tedo and I thought so.

666
00:49:56,409 --> 00:50:00,072
We surprised sundry tender glances and size which

667
00:50:00,073 --> 00:50:03,330
we interpreted as tokens of la belle pasion.

668
00:50:04,619 --> 00:50:08,150
And I promise you, the public soon had the benefit of our discovery.

669
00:50:09,479 --> 00:50:13,869
We employed it as a sort of lever to hoist our dead weights from the house.

670
00:50:15,854 --> 00:50:17,229
Dear mamma, there.

671
00:50:18,090 --> 00:50:20,212
As soon as she got an inkling of the business,

672
00:50:20,213 --> 00:50:22,930
found out that it was of an immoral tendency.

673
00:50:23,990 --> 00:50:25,409
Did you not, my lady mother?

674
00:50:26,930 --> 00:50:28,389
Certainly, my best.

675
00:50:29,259 --> 00:50:31,610
And I was quite right, depend on that.

676
00:50:32,500 --> 00:50:37,569
There are a thousand reasons why liaisons between governors and tutors should never

677
00:50:37,570 --> 00:50:40,709
be tolerated a moment in any well -regulated house.

678
00:50:41,810 --> 00:50:49,810
Firstly, oh gracious mamma, spares the enumeration, or stay, we all know them.

679
00:50:50,689 --> 00:50:53,369
Danger of bad example to innocence of childhood.

680
00:50:54,930 --> 00:50:58,529
Distractions and consequent neglect of duty on the part of the attached,

681
00:50:59,310 --> 00:51:05,169
mutual alliance and reliance, confidence, thence resulting, insolence accompanying,

682
00:51:05,950 --> 00:51:07,590
mutiny in general blow up.

683
00:51:08,424 --> 00:51:11,049
Am I right, Baroness Ingram of Ingram Park?

684
00:51:11,990 --> 00:51:15,049
My lily flower, you are right now, as always.

685
00:51:16,130 --> 00:51:17,610
Then no more need be said.

686
00:51:18,290 --> 00:51:19,290
Change the subject.

687
00:51:20,209 --> 00:51:26,830
Amy Eshton, not hearing or not heeding this joined in with her soft infantine tone.

688
00:51:27,724 --> 00:51:31,548
Luisa and I used to quiz our governess too, but she was such

689
00:51:31,549 --> 00:51:34,990
a good creature she would bear anything, nothing put her out.

690
00:51:35,529 --> 00:51:36,849
She was never cross with us.

691
00:51:37,209 --> 00:51:38,209
Was she Luisa?

692
00:51:39,090 --> 00:51:40,470
No, never.

693
00:51:41,279 --> 00:51:42,830
We might do what we pleased.

694
00:51:43,430 --> 00:51:47,529
Ransak her desk and her work box and turn her drawers inside out.

695
00:51:48,349 --> 00:51:50,250
And she was so good-natured.

696
00:51:50,790 --> 00:51:53,529
She would give us anything we asked for.

697
00:51:55,220 --> 00:52:01,790
I suppose now, said Miss Ingram curling her lips sarcastically, we shall have an

698
00:52:01,791 --> 00:52:04,830
abstract of the memoirs of all the governesses extant.

699
00:52:05,810 --> 00:52:11,151
In order to avert such a visitation, I again move the introduction of a new topic.

700
00:52:11,189 --> 00:52:13,569
Mr. Rochester, do you second my motion?

701
00:52:15,169 --> 00:52:18,750
Madam, I support you on this point, as on every other.

702
00:52:20,229 --> 00:52:23,610
Then on me, be the onus of bringing it forward.

703
00:52:24,909 --> 00:52:27,090
Senior Eduardo, are you in voice tonight?

704
00:52:28,610 --> 00:52:31,409
Donna Bianca, if you command it, I will be.

705
00:52:32,389 --> 00:52:38,169
Then, senior, I lay on you my sovereign behest to furbish up your lungs and other

706
00:52:38,170 --> 00:52:41,610
vocal organs as they will be wanted on my royal service.

707
00:52:43,099 --> 00:52:45,790
Who would not be the risio of so divine a merry?

708
00:52:47,270 --> 00:52:50,812
A fig for risio, cried she, tossing her head

709
00:52:50,812 --> 00:52:54,651
with all its curls as she moved to the piano.

710
00:52:55,139 --> 00:53:00,189
It is my opinion, the fiddler David must have been an insipid sort of fellow.

711
00:53:01,459 --> 00:53:03,229
I like blackboth well better.

712
00:53:03,970 --> 00:53:08,270
To my mind, a man is nothing without a spice of the devil in him.

713
00:53:08,970 --> 00:53:11,950
And history may say what it will of James Hepburn.

714
00:53:12,990 --> 00:53:14,049
But I have a notion.

715
00:53:14,909 --> 00:53:18,025
He was just the sort of wild, fierce, bandit hero

716
00:53:18,026 --> 00:53:21,250
whom I could have consented to gift with my hand.

717
00:53:22,875 --> 00:53:24,549
Gentlemen, you hear.

718
00:53:25,299 --> 00:53:28,150
Now, which of you most resembles Bothwell?

719
00:53:28,979 --> 00:53:29,990
cried Mr. Rochester.

720
00:53:30,869 --> 00:53:34,729
I should say the preference lies with you, responded Colonel Dent.

721
00:53:35,529 --> 00:53:37,869
On my honour, I am much obliged to you.

722
00:53:38,430 --> 00:53:39,430
Was the reply.

723
00:53:40,779 --> 00:53:45,549
Miss Ingram, who had now seated herself with proud grace at the piano,

724
00:53:46,369 --> 00:53:52,509
spreading out her snowy robes in queenly amplitude, commenced a brilliant prelude,

725
00:53:53,330 --> 00:53:54,330
talking meantime.

726
00:53:55,580 --> 00:53:58,310
She appeared to be on her high horse tonight.

727
00:53:59,750 --> 00:54:04,709
Both her words and her seemed intended to excite not only the admiration,

728
00:54:05,564 --> 00:54:07,610
but the amazement of her auditors.

729
00:54:08,509 --> 00:54:13,169
She was evidently bent on striking them as something very dashing and daring indeed.

730
00:54:15,319 --> 00:54:19,847
Oh, I am so sick of the young men of the present

731
00:54:19,848 --> 00:54:23,611
day, exclaimed she, rattling away at the instrument.

732
00:54:24,580 --> 00:54:31,490
Poor puny things, not fit to stir a step beyond Papar's park gates, nor to go even

733
00:54:31,491 --> 00:54:34,549
so far without Mama's permission and guardianship.

734
00:54:35,729 --> 00:54:39,237
Creatures so absorbed in care about their pretty

735
00:54:39,238 --> 00:54:42,390
faces and their white hands and their small feet.

736
00:54:44,099 --> 00:54:49,669
As if a man had anything to do with beauty, as if loveliness were not the

737
00:54:49,670 --> 00:54:54,150
special prerogative of woman, her legitimate a panage and heritage.

738
00:54:55,625 --> 00:55:00,770
I grant an ugly woman is a blot on the fair face of creation, but as to the

739
00:55:00,771 --> 00:55:05,349
gentleman, let them be solicitous to possess only strength and valor,

740
00:55:06,130 --> 00:55:09,389
let their motto be, hunt, shoot and fight.

741
00:55:10,250 --> 00:55:11,569
The rest is not worth a philip.

742
00:55:12,330 --> 00:55:15,189
Such should be my device, where I am man.

743
00:55:16,875 --> 00:55:20,590
Whenever I marry, she continued after a pause which none interrupted.

744
00:55:21,680 --> 00:55:26,270
I am resolved my husband shall not be arrival, but a foil to me.

745
00:55:27,560 --> 00:55:29,549
I will suffer no competitor near the throne.

746
00:55:30,369 --> 00:55:32,450
I shall exact an undivided homage.

747
00:55:33,450 --> 00:55:37,869
His devotions shall not be shared between me and the shape he sees in his mirror.

748
00:55:38,409 --> 00:55:42,169
Mr. Rochester, now sing and I will play for you.

749
00:55:43,740 --> 00:55:45,770
I am all obedience was the response.

750
00:55:47,069 --> 00:55:53,069
Here then is a Corsair song, know that I don't on Corsairs, and for that reason

751
00:55:53,395 --> 00:55:54,669
sing it conspirator.

752
00:55:56,259 --> 00:56:00,290
Commands from Miss Ingram's lips would put spirit into a mug of milk and water.

753
00:56:01,569 --> 00:56:02,569
Take care then.

754
00:56:03,409 --> 00:56:08,229
If you don't please me, I will shame you by showing how such things should be done.

755
00:56:09,569 --> 00:56:12,490
That is offering a premium on incapacity.

756
00:56:13,430 --> 00:56:14,970
I shall now endeavour to fail.

757
00:56:16,069 --> 00:56:17,709
Garde's vue on bien.

758
00:56:18,470 --> 00:56:22,790
If you air willfully, I shall devise a proportionate punishment.

759
00:56:24,729 --> 00:56:27,863
Miss Ingram ought to be clement, for she has it in her

760
00:56:27,864 --> 00:56:31,610
power to inflict a chastisement beyond mortal endurance.

761
00:56:32,349 --> 00:56:33,349
HAH!

762
00:56:33,630 --> 00:56:34,630
Explain!

763
00:56:35,169 --> 00:56:36,169
Commanded the lady.

764
00:56:37,310 --> 00:56:40,130
Pardon me, madam, no need of explanation.

765
00:56:41,060 --> 00:56:43,995
Your own fine sense must inform you that one of your frowns

766
00:56:43,996 --> 00:56:47,090
would be a sufficient substitute for capital punishment.

767
00:56:48,200 --> 00:56:51,601
Sing said she, and again touching the piano she

768
00:56:51,602 --> 00:56:54,869
commenced an accompaniment in spirited style.

769
00:56:56,009 --> 00:56:59,719
Now is my time to slip away, thought I, but the

770
00:56:59,720 --> 00:57:03,190
tones that then severed the air arrested me.

771
00:57:04,599 --> 00:57:08,369
Mrs. Fairfax had said Mr. Rochester possessed a fine voice.

772
00:57:09,169 --> 00:57:10,169
He did.

773
00:57:10,330 --> 00:57:15,290
A mellow, powerful base into which he threw his own feeling, his own force,

774
00:57:16,069 --> 00:57:21,230
finding a way through the ear to the heart, and there waking sensations strangely.

775
00:57:22,689 --> 00:57:28,610
I waited till the last deep and full vibration had expired, till the tide of

776
00:57:28,611 --> 00:57:32,689
talk checked and instant had resumed its flow.

777
00:57:33,799 --> 00:57:36,156
I then quitted my sheltered corner and made my

778
00:57:36,157 --> 00:57:38,811
exit by the side door which was fortunately near.

779
00:57:40,009 --> 00:57:42,389
Thence a narrow passage led into the hall.

780
00:57:43,229 --> 00:57:46,029
In crossing it, I perceived my sandal was loose.

781
00:57:46,930 --> 00:57:48,970
I stopped to tie it, kneeling down for that

782
00:57:48,971 --> 00:57:52,070
purpose on the mat at the foot of the staircase.

783
00:57:53,500 --> 00:57:55,950
I heard the dining room door unclose.

784
00:57:56,810 --> 00:58:01,869
A gentleman came out, rising hastily, I stood face to face with him.

785
00:58:02,270 --> 00:58:03,270
It was Mr. Rochester.

786
00:58:04,590 --> 00:58:06,130
How do you do, he asked?

787
00:58:07,389 --> 00:58:08,650
I am very well, sir.

788
00:58:09,860 --> 00:58:12,290
Why did you not come and speak to me in the room?

789
00:58:13,189 --> 00:58:16,349
I thought I might have retorted the question on

790
00:58:16,350 --> 00:58:18,991
him who put it, but I would not take that freedom.

791
00:58:19,529 --> 00:58:20,529
I answered.

792
00:58:21,610 --> 00:58:26,090
I did not wish to disturb you as you seemed engaged, sir.

793
00:58:27,729 --> 00:58:29,750
What have you been doing during my absence?

794
00:58:31,139 --> 00:58:35,151
Nothing particular, teaching Adele as usual, and getting

795
00:58:35,151 --> 00:58:38,869
a good deal paler than you were as I saw at first sight.

796
00:58:39,549 --> 00:58:40,549
What is the matter?

797
00:58:41,470 --> 00:58:42,470
Nothing at all, sir.

798
00:58:43,580 --> 00:58:45,990
Did you take any cold that night you half drowned me?

799
00:58:47,110 --> 00:58:48,110
Not the least?

800
00:58:49,229 --> 00:58:50,310
Return to the drawing room.

801
00:58:50,909 --> 00:58:52,310
You are deserting too early.

802
00:58:53,419 --> 00:58:54,529
I am tired, sir.

803
00:58:55,310 --> 00:58:56,470
He looked at me for a minute.

804
00:58:57,915 --> 00:58:59,750
And a little depressed, he said.

805
00:59:00,490 --> 00:59:01,490
What about?

806
00:59:01,529 --> 00:59:02,529
Tell me.

807
00:59:02,930 --> 00:59:04,409
Nothing, nothing, sir.

808
00:59:04,990 --> 00:59:06,290
I am not depressed.

809
00:59:07,549 --> 00:59:10,950
But I affirm that you are so much depressed that

810
00:59:10,951 --> 00:59:13,770
a few more words would bring tears to your eyes.

811
00:59:14,470 --> 00:59:19,240
Indeed, they are there now shining and swimming, and a

812
00:59:19,241 --> 00:59:23,389
bead has slipped from the lash and fallen onto the flag.

813
00:59:24,840 --> 00:59:31,069
If I had time and was not in mortal dread of some prating prig of a servant passing,

814
00:59:31,950 --> 00:59:33,790
I would know what all this means.

815
00:59:34,970 --> 00:59:40,169
Well, tonight I excuse you, but understand that so long as my visitors stay,

816
00:59:40,790 --> 00:59:43,729
I expect you to appear in the drawing room every evening.

817
00:59:44,330 --> 00:59:45,330
It is my wish.

818
00:59:45,950 --> 00:59:46,950
Don't neglect it.

819
00:59:47,919 --> 00:59:50,810
Now go, and send Sophie for Adele.

820
00:59:51,310 --> 00:59:52,310
Good night, my.

821
00:59:52,930 --> 00:59:56,069
He stopped, bit his lip, and abruptly left me.
